57-46a2-9369-5f34f4c7fd49"},{"text":"If you want good weather, you can't go wrong with Spain.","bold_text_offsets":[[36,44]],"type":"example","id":"bebd8b69-6cd6-4d78-9a8c-3aa1838cefab"},{"text":"I just don't know what went wrong!","ref":"2012, Amy Keating Rogers, The Last Roundup, spoken by Derpy Hooves:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[23,33]],"id":"ce866a7b-8c36-44fd-8c5b-3d9f7d273764"},{"text":"Johnson explained that absolute gauging assumed that everything that could go wrong would go wrong at the same time, resulting in the train hitting the platform. In contrast, probabilistic gauging says that everything can go wrong, but not at the same time.","ref":"2023 April 19, Philip Haigh, “Gauging ways to ensure rail freight gains more paths”, in RAIL, number 981, page 45:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[75,83],[90,98],[222,230]],"id":"9e9ddebb-c2a2-4f05-8724-98a54a9e11b7"}],"categories":["English idioms","English intransitive verbs","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["worsen","worsen"],["fail","fail"],["amiss","amiss"],["outcome","outcome"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"atrophy","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"break down","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"crack","source":"Thesaurus:worsen","tags":["archaic"]},{"word":"decline","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"deteriorate","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"degenerate","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"devolve","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"confound","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"fade","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"fall off","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go bad","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go downhill","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go left","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go off","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go pear-shaped","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go sideways","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go south","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go to hell","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go to pot","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go to seed","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go to the dogs","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"go wrong","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"lapse","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"molder","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"pejorate","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"retrograde","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"suffer","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"spend","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"sweal","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"shrivel","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"tabefy","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"wither","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"wither away","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"wane","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"wanse","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"},{"word":"worsen","source":"Thesaurus:worsen"}],"raw_glosses":["(intransitive, idiomatic) To worsen; to fail or go amiss; to have a bad outcome."],"glosses":["To worsen; to fail or go amiss; to have a bad outcome."],"tags":["idiomatic","intransitive"],"id":"bb208bf1-490d-40ee-b228-bc4fa201e760"},{"examples":[{"text":"The vending machine went wrong and dispensed five cans of drink at once.","bold_text_offsets":[[20,30]],"type":"example","id":"830a6b45-2eb6-44bf-9cf1-f1136f97b7f1"}],"categories":["English idioms","English intransitive verbs","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["malfunction","malfunction"]],"raw_glosses":["(intransitive, idiomatic) To malfunction."],"glosses":["To malfunction."],"tags":["idiomatic","intransitive"],"id":"2c569ee5-9b29-4995-b835-6f0184dd373d"},{"examples":[{"text":"Mr. Blue Sky / Please tell us why / You had to hide away for so long (so long) / Where did we go wrong?","ref":"1977, Electric Light Orchestra, “Mr. Blue Sky”, in Out of the Blue:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[94,102]],"id":"f21ed54f-c7bb-4e4c-9c0a-cc4802dda44d"}],"categories":["English idioms","English intransitive verbs","English terms with q